Subject: Cantor FPGA Lowering Profile

Description: Canonical non-executable SJS contract for evaluating optional future FPGA realizations of eligible Cantor Process IR kernels. It defines stable eligibility, interface, evidence, admission-separation, and correspondence obligations but authorizes no hardware implementation or target activity.

@ [FPGA_source_manifest] C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-08-05_simula_inference_control_correspondence\Source_Document_Manifest.sop
@ [processing_input_manifest] C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-08-05_cantor_deterministic_runtime_activation\SJS_Processing_Input_Manifest.sop
@ [exploded_specification] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\exploded\Cantor_FPGA_Lowering_Profile.exploded.sop
@ [registry] C:\Project\Cantor\narrative\registries\Cantor_FPGA_Lowering_Profile_Registry.sop
@ [phase_lock] C:\Project\Cantor\narrative\registries\Cantor_FPGA_Lowering_Profile_Phase_Lock.sop

& [CanonicalIdentity] is exact
  + [canonical_uuid] is 5f312b2e-8839-46f6-a09e-e9d6e67e55fa
  + [profile] is cantor-fpga-lowering-profile/0.1
  + [requirement_set] is CFLP-001 through CFLP-024
  + [authority_grade] is non_executable_correspondence_contract
  + [canonical_source_specification] is this file

& [SemanticLayerBoundary] is permanent
  + SOP declares meaning, purpose, identity, constraints, and proof
  + Cantor Process Procedure declares model and human-facing process behavior
  + canonical Cantor Process IR is the only eligible future semantic lowering input
  + hardware descriptions and bitstreams are derived target artifacts
  - never: allow VHDL, Verilog, SystemVerilog, HLS C or C++, CIRCT, netlist, or vendor IR to redefine canonical semantics

& [DerivedTargetArtifactContract] preserves semantic precedence
  + every future HDL, HLS, compiler IR, netlist, constraint, firmware, driver, and bitstream artefact cites its exact canonical Process IR input and transform identity
  + target diagnostics, optimizations, physical layout, and tool metadata remain derived evidence
  + no derived artefact may weaken source effects, bounds, ordering, identity, or proof obligations

& [EligibleInputContract] is narrow
  + finite fixed-width values, bounded collections, explicit immutable process states, bounded queues, declared maximum steps, deterministic scheduling, and effectless operations
  + no recursion, dynamic allocation, OS call, arbitrary code loading, hidden storage, live provider, model call, or external effect
  + procedure and IR must already be separately admitted for the intended software context

& [KernelEligibility] is an explicit disposition
  + eligibility checks finite types, static bounds, deterministic scheduling, effect class, queue capacity, termination, interface support, semantic-trace support, and software-reference availability
  + eligible means suitable for profiling or target-specific consideration and never means synthesized, performant, correct, signed, or loadable
  + any unsupported construct produces an ineligible result with evidence rather than partial lowering

& [ProfilingGate] precedes target work
  + candidate states invocation frequency, latency, throughput, power, area, determinism, or isolation objective
  + measured software reference baseline and accelerator alternatives are required
  + only a stable material bottleneck or isolation need may seed a target-specific addendum
  + no present kernel is selected

& [CandidateKernelSet] is illustrative only
  + digest and CRC pipelines
  + signed-catalogue lookup
  + bounded relation filtering and score accumulation
  + bounded graph-frontier expansion
  + deterministic arbitration, FIFO messaging, barrier accounting, and trace emission
  + inclusion here is not profiling evidence or implementation authority

& [HostBoundary] retains semantic and effect responsibility
  + model calls, semantic judgment, procedure admission, policy, explanation, filesystem, network, database, provider, Calendar, Git, credentials, and external effects remain host-side
  + device consumes only exact typed bounded requests and admitted artefacts

& [RealizationProfiles] are distinct
  + FPGA interpreter is stable admitted circuitry executing signed bounded IR or bytecode as data
  + native FPGA realization is dedicated circuitry derived from one stable admitted procedure or kernel
  + interpreter evidence and admission cannot support native realization claims
  + software or procedure admission cannot support hardware compilation or loading claims

& [HostDeviceInterface] must be explicit in a future addendum
  + typed versioned request, response, fault, control, and trace channels
  + exact schema, width, endianness, framing, backpressure, fairness, deadlock, overflow, reset, and cancellation semantics
  + bounded FIFO or equivalent handshake behavior
  + no interface is presently selected

& [SchedulerCorrespondence] is semantic rather than cycle identical
  + logical event ordering and stable tie-break match the software reference
  + normalized semantic result and trace correspond for identical inputs
  + physical clocks, pipeline stages, stalls, and cycle counts may differ as telemetry

& [HardwareFaultContract] is future mandatory evidence
  + resource exhaustion, timeout, reset, partial response, transport fault, stale invocation, and correspondence failure are typed fail-closed outcomes
  + no partial result can be represented as admitted completion

& [CorrespondenceProof] is multi-level
  + identical normalized inputs to software reference and hardware candidate
  + identical typed semantic result and normalized semantic trace within declared physical telemetry exclusions
  + IR validation, golden tests, RTL or HLS simulation, applicable properties, synthesis, timing, resources, and target integration evidence
  + final output equality alone is insufficient

& [ArtifactIdentityChain] is exact
  + future compiler, IR, RTL, netlist, constraints, report, firmware, driver, and bitstream bind digest, toolchain, target, provenance, diagnostics, and status
  + every transform records before, after, loss, correspondence, and invalidation

& [AdmissionSeparation] prevents authority laundering
  + source proposal, procedure admission, IR eligibility, hardware compilation, bitstream signing, device loading, and runtime invocation are distinct dispositions
  + model-generated HDL, HLS, constraints, or procedure source may be candidate input only
  + no candidate self-verifies, self-signs, self-loads, or grants device authority

& [ModelAuthorshipBoundary] applies to every hardware candidate
  + a model may propose IR transforms, HDL, HLS, constraints, tests, or documentation only as attributed candidate material
  + model authorship grants no semantic correspondence, verification, synthesis, signing, credential, device, or loading authority
  + generated artefacts follow the same target-specific evidence and admission path as human-authored candidates

& [TargetSpecificAddendumGate] blocks execution
  + future preserved source must name device, board, vendor, toolchain, versions, interface, memory, clocks, reset, constraints, side channels, isolation, secure boot, signing, keys, loading, rollback, and physical acceptance
  + target addendum requires its own SJS signature and separate implementation claim
  + absent addendum means no HDL, HLS, simulation, synthesis, bitstream, driver, purchase, loading, or device action

& [NonClaimSet] is explicit
  + no literal shared model hidden state
  + no on-FPGA LLM inference
  + no semantic accuracy improvement from speed
  + no selected language, vendor, toolchain, board, device, frequency, performance, cost, or deployment
  + no current executable FPGA frontier

